                     /note="Members of this protein family, MftF, are
                     glycosyltransferases, members of PF00535 (glycosyl
                     transferase family 2). The encoding gene is found as part
                     of the mycofactocin cassette, in Mycobacterium
                     tuberculosis, many other Actinobacteria, and occasional
                     members of other lineages. Mycofactocin itself, a putative
                     redox carrier, is a heavily modified derivative of the
                     C-terminal Val-Tyr dipeptide of the mycofactocin precursor
